  <div class="page prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>Ryan D. Lewis</h1>
    <p class="lede">Ryan is an explorer and photographer whose work centers on Kentucky’s Red River Gorge and Clifty Wilderness.</p>

    <p>Red River Gorge Hiker grew from the time Ryan spends hiking, backpacking, camping, searching for remote features, and returning to familiar places in changing weather and seasons.</p>

    <p>The photographs on this site are tied to those experiences. A summer storm produced the double rainbow over Eagle’s Point Buttress. Severe winter conditions transformed Red-byrd Arch. A campsite revealed an unexpected sunrise. Remote waterfall exploration led to the discovery and documentation of Splatter Falls.</p>

    <p>Ryan personally owns the copyright to his photographs. Red River Gorge Hiker is the public brand through which he shares the work, the stories behind it, and selected prints and puzzles.</p>

    <h2>More photographs will follow</h2>
    <p>The launch collection is the beginning. Future work will continue to reflect the places, weather, seasons, and experiences Ryan encounters in the Gorge.</p>
